# Text is checked out with LF on every platform. Source files, fixtures and
# templates are read by tests that pin their bytes, hashes or exact text (a
# canonical wire, a frontmatter fence, a source scan), and a Windows checkout's
# CRLF made each of them fail without any code being wrong.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Captured terminal bytes carry their own CR/LF and escapes.
*.bin binary
zo-ide/crates/zo-ide/tests/fixtures/codex-capture-*.txt -text

# Windows scripts are read by cmd and PowerShell, which want CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
